(406462, 34883, 5391, '<td valign="top">I thought this was hysterical and extremely creative.  I gave it an 8.  Good job of "seeing".  :)  Terribly disappointed that it didn''t do better, but I think a lot of people don''t look long enough to "get" some of the more creative shots here.</td>', 'I thought this was hysterical and extremely creative.  I gave it an 8.  Good job of "seeing".  :)  Terribly disappointed that it didn''t do better, but I think a lot of people don''t look long enough to "get" some of the more creative shots here.', '2003-09-01 16:14:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(406468, 34538, 7778, '<td valign="top">Powerful and contemporary interpretation of the challenge topic! The dizzying perspective proves apt here to achieve a sheer monolithic impact. The lighting is kept suitably harsh to prevent a too easy and  <i> pleasing</i> impression. There are no distracting technical flaws, that I can detect. Outstanding!<br/> <br/><i>The Colour of Money</i> would make a plausible an alternate title (for prosperity), even though your choice is a good one for the challenge, IMO.<br/> <br/><b> Zeus''s Top Pic(k)s: 2nd Place </b><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-09-01 15:25:56.</i></td>', 'Powerful and contemporary interpretation of the challenge topic! The dizzying perspective proves apt here to achieve a sheer monolithic impact. The lighting is kept suitably harsh to prevent a too easy and   pleasing impression. There are no distracting technical flaws, that I can detect. Outstanding! The Colour of Money would make a plausible an alternate title (for prosperity), even though your choice is a good one for the challenge, IMO.  Zeus''s Top Pic(k)s: 2nd Place ', '2003-09-01 16:24:40.000000', '2003-09-01 16:25:56.000000', 0),
