(406574, 34832, 259, '<td valign="top">mark me down for the third person that thinks you were screwed.</td>', 'mark me down for the third person that thinks you were screwed.', '2003-09-01 18:55:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(406852, 34873, 1647, '<td valign="top">The monument is certainly interesting and the frozen water splash looks great.  It''s a shame the weather wasn''t more on your side - the sky has a lot of glare and therefore blends with the fish too much.  The composition is fairly good - if the sky was a nice blue colour I would have tried taking the shot from closer to the ground, placing the fish in the sky effectively and looking along the water rather than down onto it.<br/> <br/>It was probably the flatness of colour that hurt your score most since the rest of the photo is quite good.</td>', 'The monument is certainly interesting and the frozen water splash looks great.  It''s a shame the weather wasn''t more on your side - the sky has a lot of glare and therefore blends with the fish too much.  The composition is fairly good - if the sky was a nice blue colour I would have tried taking the shot from closer to the ground, placing the fish in the sky effectively and looking along the water rather than down onto it. It was probably the flatness of colour that hurt your score most since the rest of the photo is quite good.', '2003-09-02 02:32:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(406874, 34823, 6912, '<td valign="top">Tank you for all your nice comments. This statue is itself golden, and is nicely illuminated at night, worth seeing a lot! Cheers, Nasti<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-09-02 03:42:19.</i></td>', 'Tank you for all your nice comments. This statue is itself golden, and is nicely illuminated at night, worth seeing a lot! Cheers, Nasti', '2003-09-02 03:31:26.000000', '2003-09-02 04:42:19.000000', 0),
(406888, 34768, 6999, '<td valign="top">This is getting ridiculous - I only ever get your photos for the Critique Club Anna. <br/> <br/>This is such a very literal shot, so very straight-on, and I think it''s suffered for that. Sure, it gives a sense f place to the monument, but the windows and the brickwork of the building behind really draw the eye away, and make it difficult to discern any detail in the statue.<br/> <br/>As with Pisaman''s comment, I feel that you might have sacrificed too much to keep the flags in shot: and what also annoys me is that the figures in the statue look so intersting that I want ot see more detail there. I wonder if you tried a shot looking up at the figures, with the flags in the background? <br/> <br/>I think it may be a touch over-exposed too - the highlight area, and there are a lot of them at that time of day, seem too white, blown out to me. There is also some barrel distortion around the edges - the linews of the building, and of the outer flagpoles are curved, presumably due to shooting at the widest angle: try using a touch of the zoom to correct that.<br/> <br/>All the best<br/> <br/>Ed</td>', 'This is getting ridiculous - I only ever get your photos for the Critique Club Anna.  This is such a very literal shot, so very straight-on, and I think it''s suffered for that. Sure, it gives a sense f place to the monument, but the windows and the brickwork of the building behind really draw the eye away, and make it difficult to discern any detail in the statue. As with Pisaman''s comment, I feel that you might have sacrificed too much to keep the flags in shot: and what also annoys me is that the figures in the statue look so intersting that I want ot see more detail there. I wonder if you tried a shot looking up at the figures, with the flags in the background?  I think it may be a touch over-exposed too - the highlight area, and there are a lot of them at that time of day, seem too white, blown out to me. There is also some barrel distortion around the edges - the linews of the building, and of the outer flagpoles are curved, presumably due to shooting at the widest angle: try using a touch of the zoom to correct that. All the best Ed', '2003-09-02 05:25:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(406909, 34875, 11401, '<td valign="top">Congrats, very nice pic.</td>', 'Congrats, very nice pic.', '2003-09-02 06:12:58.000000', NULL, 0),
