(407131, 34727, 8306, '<td valign="top">awesome photo!</td>', 'awesome photo!', '2003-09-02 13:57:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(407173, 34877, 527, '<td valign="top">Very nice job Eddy! I love shots like this. A well deserved win.</td>', 'Very nice job Eddy! I love shots like this. A well deserved win.', '2003-09-02 15:07:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(407177, 34875, 527, '<td valign="top">Great job Mag! You chose the perfect lighting to compliment the monument and trees and the cropping works very well too. -T</td>', 'Great job Mag! You chose the perfect lighting to compliment the monument and trees and the cropping works very well too. -T', '2003-09-02 15:12:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(407427, 34867, 10084, '<td valign="top">Beautiful curved lines makes the composition very interesting. Without including the lines of the rail on the stairs yours eyes look right at the metallic shape that says "Walt Disney Concert Hall". On the rightside either include more of the sky or keep it out of the composition. Cropping in closer will do the trick. On the leftside of the photograph. The side in rather interesting with the straight lines. It''s a bit dark compared to the main part of the picture. I think putting more of it in the background would bring out the center curves out even more. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Beautiful curved lines makes the composition very interesting. Without including the lines of the rail on the stairs yours eyes look right at the metallic shape that says "Walt Disney Concert Hall". On the rightside either include more of the sky or keep it out of the composition. Cropping in closer will do the trick. On the leftside of the photograph. The side in rather interesting with the straight lines. It''s a bit dark compared to the main part of the picture. I think putting more of it in the background would bring out the center curves out even more.  ', '2003-09-02 21:22:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(407500, 34807, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>This is simply a stunning nightime photo.  The focus is excellent as is the color and the lighting.  <br/> <br/>I sat here and tried to find something I would change about the photo but honestly there isn''t a thing.  I would however love to see other angles of this if you have them.  <br/> <br/>Simply fantastic Gary!<br/> <br/>Almost forgot yes, it also does fit the challenge.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', '*Critique Club* This is simply a stunning nightime photo.  The focus is excellent as is the color and the lighting.   I sat here and tried to find something I would change about the photo but honestly there isn''t a thing.  I would however love to see other angles of this if you have them.   Simply fantastic Gary! Almost forgot yes, it also does fit the challenge. Anna', '2003-09-02 22:53:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(408069, 34875, 2716, '<td valign="top">Mag!  Great work.  Congrats on a non green or purple ribbon.  :)</td>', 'Mag!  Great work.  Congrats on a non green or purple ribbon.  :)', '2003-09-03 08:14:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(408121, 34875, 472, '<td valign="top">Thanks all friends and well-wishers.  And you people who are normally friendly and well-wishing, but conspicuously absent here, you are missed.</td>', 'Thanks all friends and well-wishers.  And you people who are normally friendly and well-wishing, but conspicuously absent here, you are missed.', '2003-09-03 09:49:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(410415, 34819, 3540, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/>By Inspzil<br/> <br/>Composition - Subject wise, I don''t see how this is meeting the challenge.  I''m thinking of these things more like characters than monuments.  But I think that''s really secondary here.  I don''t really understand this interpretation though as a picture on the whole.  I find the background to be very busy.  I think this would''ve been a good picture to take the ants perspective and shoot straight up on this one.  The sky looks like a good fitting background for this.  I think that the angle is a little odd too that this picture was taken with.  I''m not really understanding that either.  It doesn''t really seem to accomplish anything except make the photo a little different than the norm, but I can''t say its for the better necessarily.  It is however, at a considerable enough angle that we can tell its on purpose and not just a little mistake on your part.<br/> <br/>Technical - This isn''t a badly taken pic.  The colors are pretty good and its very clear.  With that much camera, it really shouldn''t have too many technical problems.  I''m not sure how the original looks compared to the final image, but this seems okay.<br/> <br/>Overall - I just flat out don''t get this picture.  I''m not seeing how its relating to the challenge topic and the angle is throwing me for a bit of a loop too.  I''m not particularly fond of this picture for these reasons.  Good luck, take care - Bob</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique ClubBy Inspzil Composition - Subject wise, I don''t see how this is meeting the challenge.  I''m thinking of these things more like characters than monuments.  But I think that''s really secondary here.  I don''t really understand this interpretation though as a picture on the whole.  I find the background to be very busy.  I think this would''ve been a good picture to take the ants perspective and shoot straight up on this one.  The sky looks like a good fitting background for this.  I think that the angle is a little odd too that this picture was taken with.  I''m not really understanding that either.  It doesn''t really seem to accomplish anything except make the photo a little different than the norm, but I can''t say its for the better necessarily.  It is however, at a considerable enough angle that we can tell its on purpose and not just a little mistake on your part. Technical - This isn''t a badly taken pic.  The colors are pretty good and its very clear.  With that much camera, it really shouldn''t have too many technical problems.  I''m not sure how the original looks compared to the final image, but this seems okay. Overall - I just flat out don''t get this picture.  I''m not seeing how its relating to the challenge topic and the angle is throwing me for a bit of a loop too.  I''m not particularly fond of this picture for these reasons.  Good luck, take care - Bob', '2003-09-05 06:22:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(411107, 34612, 7778, '<td valign="top">Since several comments were based on (false) assumptions regarding processing, I want to point out, that this image was inverted, as picked up on by hughletheren and, probably by a few others as well . It is lightly cropped, and conservative (very minimal) fine tuning was applied to the whole image via brightness, contrast and hue, mainly to bring out texture.<br/> <br/>I wish some voters would not make assumptions without having the facts. A question mark in lieu of the period at the end of a sentence would reflect the same view, without creating a need for correction.<br/> <br/>Regardless of this, I appreciated all comments.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-09-07 13:15:06.</i></td>', 'Since several comments were based on (false) assumptions regarding processing, I want to point out, that this image was inverted, as picked up on by hughletheren and, probably by a few others as well . It is lightly cropped, and conservative (very minimal) fine tuning was applied to the whole image via brightness, contrast and hue, mainly to bring out texture. I wish some voters would not make assumptions without having the facts. A question mark in lieu of the period at the end of a sentence would reflect the same view, without creating a need for correction. Regardless of this, I appreciated all comments.', '2003-09-06 13:25:20.000000', '2003-09-07 14:15:06.000000', 0),
(411195, 34318, 1143, '<td valign="top">Dang. 31st? It was my favorite for the challenge. Proving once again that the voters aren''t always right.</td>', 'Dang. 31st? It was my favorite for the challenge. Proving once again that the voters aren''t always right.', '2003-09-06 19:10:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(411481, 34832, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Very nice image, excellent focus and detail.  Lighting worked well here.  Only thing I don''t like is the white background it is just to white and there is nothing there.</td>', '*Critique Club* Very nice image, excellent focus and detail.  Lighting worked well here.  Only thing I don''t like is the white background it is just to white and there is nothing there.', '2003-09-07 12:38:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(411484, 34727, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Beautiful photo, the sunset adds so much drama to the photo.  The trees on each side make for a wonderful framing.  Your reflection is near perfect as well.  In all honesty you did a fantastic job on this.  Well done.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', '*Critique Club* Beautiful photo, the sunset adds so much drama to the photo.  The trees on each side make for a wonderful framing.  Your reflection is near perfect as well.  In all honesty you did a fantastic job on this.  Well done. Anna', '2003-09-07 12:43:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(411577, 34817, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>The statue itself needs a little more defination, as it is lacking shadowing and depth.  However the palm tree behind it makes up greatly for it.  The tree gives the entire statue an appearence of a "halo" around the mother and babe much like many of the old masters have painted the MaDonna.  <br/> <br/>Your composition is very good and you might improve on it overall but cropping in at the bottom and cutting out part of the base.  There seems to be a line almost created by the bottom of the trees and the placard of the statue.  Cutting that little bit out might improve a little on it.<br/> <br/>Overall it fits the challenge well.  Nicely done.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', '*Critique Club* The statue itself needs a little more defination, as it is lacking shadowing and depth.  However the palm tree behind it makes up greatly for it.  The tree gives the entire statue an appearence of a "halo" around the mother and babe much like many of the old masters have painted the MaDonna.   Your composition is very good and you might improve on it overall but cropping in at the bottom and cutting out part of the base.  There seems to be a line almost created by the bottom of the trees and the placard of the statue.  Cutting that little bit out might improve a little on it. Overall it fits the challenge well.  Nicely done. Anna', '2003-09-07 16:43:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(424596, 34318, 8860, '<td valign="top">Superb shot, great composition and viewpoint, intersting subject too. Love the lighting and sky tones. And 31st? My only criticism is perhaps the heavy border - I''d like to see the balance without it.</td>', 'Superb shot, great composition and viewpoint, intersting subject too. Love the lighting and sky tones. And 31st? My only criticism is perhaps the heavy border - I''d like to see the balance without it.', '2003-09-20 05:26:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(460754, 34863, 12332, '<td valign="top">Hello from a former Saratogian.  The 7th shot I ever took with a 35 mm (back in 1976) was at this memorial. (Yours is much better!!)  Here''s another possible shot for you, should you choose to accept it.  <br/> <br/>Under the footbridge to SPAC is a hill that has built up over the years from a sulphur-heavy spring.  The 5th shot I ever took was there, and is one of my favorite, if imperfect, pictures.  <a href="//community.webshots.com/photo/50280443/54074381BwAXYo" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">sulphur hill reflection</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-23 22:41:12.</i></td>', 'Hello from a former Saratogian.  The 7th shot I ever took with a 35 mm (back in 1976) was at this memorial. (Yours is much better!!)  Here''s another possible shot for you, should you choose to accept it.   Under the footbridge to SPAC is a hill that has built up over the years from a sulphur-heavy spring.  The 5th shot I ever took was there, and is one of my favorite, if imperfect, pictures.  sulphur hill reflection', '2003-10-23 23:39:55.000000', '2003-10-23 23:41:12.000000', 0),
(463410, 34666, 11114, '<td valign="top">He is great - no doubt - but I wonder how you interpret the following scripture from Deuteronomy 5:8 <br/> <br/>"You shall not make for yourself an idol in the form of anything in heaven above or on the earth beneath or in the waters below.  9 You shall not bow down to them or worship them;<br/> <br/>PS  If this is a sore point of something that you''d rather not discuss, simply do not reply.  I''m not interested in stirring up animosity.<br/>If, however, you''re interested to discuss it - then I guess I''ll be hearing from you!</td>', 'He is great - no doubt - but I wonder how you interpret the following scripture from Deuteronomy 5:8  "You shall not make for yourself an idol in the form of anything in heaven above or on the earth beneath or in the waters below.  9 You shall not bow down to them or worship them; PS  If this is a sore point of something that you''d rather not discuss, simply do not reply.  I''m not interested in stirring up animosity.If, however, you''re interested to discuss it - then I guess I''ll be hearing from you!', '2003-10-27 12:55:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(464484, 34666, 772, '<td valign="top">Well, If you would like my interpetation of that specific verse taken completely out of context, I would suppose that it means that it is against God''s word to create a statue (idol), or any other likeness for the purpose of worship.  However, I don''t interpret it this way when it''s put in context of the ten commandments.  I don''t particularly care to discuss the ramifications of individual bits of scripture that are taken out of context.  I prefer to evaluate them on a larger scale and in context with the overall teachings in conjunction with what I have been taught throughout my own life.  :)</td>', 'Well, If you would like my interpetation of that specific verse taken completely out of context, I would suppose that it means that it is against God''s word to create a statue (idol), or any other likeness for the purpose of worship.  However, I don''t interpret it this way when it''s put in context of the ten commandments.  I don''t particularly care to discuss the ramifications of individual bits of scripture that are taken out of context.  I prefer to evaluate them on a larger scale and in context with the overall teachings in conjunction with what I have been taught throughout my own life.  :)', '2003-10-28 12:43:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(493296, 34883, 13403, '<td valign="top">i love the huge phallic symbol.   heh</td>', 'i love the huge phallic symbol.   heh', '2003-11-24 07:14:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(508046, 34867, 8860, '<td valign="top">Well chosen subject and nicely taken shot. A striking form indeed. I would perhaps have allowed either more space to the right or cropped out the background altogether, which would redirect focus even more onto the shapes created.</td>', 'Well chosen subject and nicely taken shot. A striking form indeed. I would perhaps have allowed either more space to the right or cropped out the background altogether, which would redirect focus even more onto the shapes created.', '2003-12-09 14:43:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(517436, 34867, 8054, '<td valign="top">I know this is late but I''d like to thank everyone for their comments about this image. I took a break from DPC just because I thought this picture was doing so well and then no ribbon. I was devastated to say the least. Anyway, I came back and cast some votes in the shapes challenge because I figured I''d better vote before I submit to a challenge, right?  :)<br/> <br/>Anywho, I''d like to say thanks, again, for all the useful and constructive comments and so sorry that it took me so long to reply to everyone.</td>', 'I know this is late but I''d like to thank everyone for their comments about this image. I took a break from DPC just because I thought this picture was doing so well and then no ribbon. I was devastated to say the least. Anyway, I came back and cast some votes in the shapes challenge because I figured I''d better vote before I submit to a challenge, right?  :) Anywho, I''d like to say thanks, again, for all the useful and constructive comments and so sorry that it took me so long to reply to everyone.', '2003-12-19 01:57:51.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(530948, 34763, 15653, '<td valign="top">A photo of someone else''s art is not art in itself.  It needs to be juxtaposed with something else to create unique interest.</td>', 'A photo of someone else''s art is not art in itself.  It needs to be juxtaposed with something else to create unique interest.', '2004-01-03 20:13:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(704240, 34867, 21179, '<td valign="top">fyi, the panels are made of titanium. i would say that is one of mr. gehry''s favorite materials to use on his buildings.<br/>back to the phot, it''s a great shot, i would have brought the viewing angle up a bit higher so that the railing would show some movement to echo the building. At the current viewing angle the railing starts to come off the page, but then turns into a hrozontal element. if it came out of the page it would be much more dramatic and really reinforce the movement going on in the photo.<br/>you should try photographing this on a gloomy/ rainy day. the titanium takes on many moods due to weather. it''s always an interesting subject.<br/></td>', 'fyi, the panels are made of titanium. i would say that is one of mr. gehry''s favorite materials to use on his buildings.back to the phot, it''s a great shot, i would have brought the viewing angle up a bit higher so that the railing would show some movement to echo the building. At the current viewing angle the railing starts to come off the page, but then turns into a hrozontal element. if it came out of the page it would be much more dramatic and really reinforce the movement going on in the photo.you should try photographing this on a gloomy/ rainy day. the titanium takes on many moods due to weather. it''s always an interesting subject.', '2004-05-07 13:59:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(731611, 34221, 22054, '<td valign="top">please make this a print i love the photo. and what is this a monument of?</td>', 'please make this a print i love the photo. and what is this a monument of?', '2004-05-22 19:40:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(778502, 34863, 4492, '<td valign="top">Of course this is really just a picture of someone else''s artwork - you just took a fairly routine picture of it.</td>', 'Of course this is really just a picture of someone else''s artwork - you just took a fairly routine picture of it.', '2004-06-24 20:41:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1199619, 34666, 12809, '<td valign="top">Simple, but powerful.  Great choice for b&amp;w.  The black bg is terrific, it really makes this a work of art.</td>', 'Simple, but powerful.  Great choice for b&w.  The black bg is terrific, it really makes this a work of art.', '2005-02-28 18:21:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(1625264, 34915, 42712, '<td valign="top">I was just wondering if you have any more information about this fountain. I am currently doing some research on these fountains which were donated to cities all over the country. You can find out more at //www.electronicvalley.org/derby/quiz/pages/wateringtrough.htm.<br/></td>', 'I was just wondering if you have any more information about this fountain. I am currently doing some research on these fountains which were donated to cities all over the country. You can find out more at //www.electronicvalley.org/derby/quiz/pages/wateringtrough.htm.', '2005-08-20 00:03:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1629425, 34863, 34659, '<td valign="top">This is really a beautifully composed shot.  The lighting is a little harsh, but the composition more than makes up for any failings there.  Have you experimented with the lighting settings in processing (i.e., backlighting, midtones, shadows, etc.)?  I think this could pop even more with a little more contrast.</td>', 'This is really a beautifully composed shot.  The lighting is a little harsh, but the composition more than makes up for any failings there.  Have you experimented with the lighting settings in processing (i.e., backlighting, midtones, shadows, etc.)?  I think this could pop even more with a little more contrast.', '2005-08-22 01:07:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6622318, 34491, 141982, '<td valign="top">Today I was so heavy in heart .. like a massive weight. A break in the joy and thanksgiving I have at this time of year .. to pray for my friends that have lost a child. I lost my dad a couple months back .. but I would imagine nothing compares to the loss of a child :(, and especially near Christmas.  But as I prayed, I was looking to put a pic on facebook to go with a prayer. A prayer that sat heavy with no words .. only knowing that God would do what I couldn''t put words for .. and comfort a heart in a way I could only dream of.  So I sat in front of Google "Image" , as I often do .. looking for a pic that would capture attention to go with teh prayer. And usually I can spent a great deal of time typing in word after word that might spark what I am feeling, and am image to relate it. NOT TODAY. I prayed and put in angel of hope .. cause I wanted the spirit of hope to be imparted to my friends that I love so dearly .. and this photo jumped out! IT''S WONDERFUL. I know nothing of this site, I cant even find the photographers name? yup, I''m an idiot :/ ..  but I wanted to say that I thought it''s very nice, adn that I''m sitting here weeping becasue it came IMMEDIATELY  .. which is impossible with how large the internet is!!!!!!! God touched my heart today, while lifting up others .. and thru your picture it was made manifest to my heart. Merry Christmas to you and yours. Wish I could see this momument in person</td>', 'Today I was so heavy in heart .. like a massive weight. A break in the joy and thanksgiving I have at this time of year .. to pray for my friends that have lost a child. I lost my dad a couple months back .. but I would imagine nothing compares to the loss of a child :(, and especially near Christmas.  But as I prayed, I was looking to put a pic on facebook to go with a prayer. A prayer that sat heavy with no words .. only knowing that God would do what I couldn''t put words for .. and comfort a heart in a way I could only dream of.  So I sat in front of Google "Image" , as I often do .. looking for a pic that would capture attention to go with teh prayer. And usually I can spent a great deal of time typing in word after word that might spark what I am feeling, and am image to relate it. NOT TODAY. I prayed and put in angel of hope .. cause I wanted the spirit of hope to be imparted to my friends that I love so dearly .. and this photo jumped out! IT''S WONDERFUL. I know nothing of this site, I cant even find the photographers name? yup, I''m an idiot :/ ..  but I wanted to say that I thought it''s very nice, adn that I''m sitting here weeping becasue it came IMMEDIATELY  .. which is impossible with how large the internet is!!!!!!! God touched my heart today, while lifting up others .. and thru your picture it was made manifest to my heart. Merry Christmas to you and yours. Wish I could see this momument in person', '2011-12-20 11:49:31.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
